# PR Verification — Hard Procedural Rule

Never declare a PR "ready to merge" off the back of unit tests + CI alone. Run the full verification battery first.

## AUTOMATED ENFORCEMENT (run this, don't rely on memory)

This rule was missed more than a dozen times because it depended on the agent *remembering* to walk the battery. It no longer does. The battery is now mechanical:

The branch must be **fully end-to-end tested BEFORE its PR is created** — not after. One command enforces the whole thing:

```bash
scripts/pr_battery.sh            # default site myschools.localhost
```

It runs in two stages and only writes the sentinel `.cursor/.pr-battery-pass` (stamped with the **current commit SHA**) when BOTH pass:

- **STAGE 1 — local fast checks:** lint/pre-commit, unit tests + coverage, role×surface branch-desk matrix, coverage floor, live HTTP smoke on the dev site. Fast feedback before spending CI minutes.
- **STAGE 2 — CI end-to-end gate:** requires the branch to be pushed and the **CI workflow to be terminal-green for the EXACT current commit**. CI *is* the full battery — fresh-install (drop → new-site → install-app → migrate), seed, branch matrix, live HTTP battery, and **Playwright browser e2e**. We do not fake fresh-install/browser locally; we require the real CI run to be green for this commit. CI now triggers on `feature/**` pushes (see `.github/workflows/ci.yml`) precisely so this runs **before** the PR exists.

**A Cursor hook blocks PR finalisation without it.** `.cursor/hooks.json` → `.cursor/hooks/require-battery.sh` gates `gh pr create`, `gh pr merge`, `gh pr ready` (`failClosed: true`). If the sentinel SHA ≠ HEAD SHA the command is held with `permission: ask`. **Do not bypass** — re-run `scripts/pr_battery.sh`.

**Workflow:** make changes → commit → `git push` → `scripts/pr_battery.sh` (Stage 1 local, then waits for CI green on this commit) → `gh pr create`. Any new commit invalidates the sentinel and re-fires the gate — intended; re-run on the new commit. `SKIP_CI_WAIT=1` runs Stage 1 only and does **not** write the sentinel (so it can't satisfy the gate).

**Judgement-only items** (not auto-gated, confirm in the PR body): PDF round-trip *if* a print format changed; and the **per-phase 5a/5b/5c trio** — a local Playwright run (paste pass count), a manual dev-site browser walk with attached screenshots, and a written spec-completeness audit. These are **mandatory every phase that touches a browser-facing surface**, not optional extras (see the battery items 5a/5b/5c and the Phase 11 PR #24 incident below). "CI ran Playwright" satisfies none of them.

## Why (this rule has been triggered FIVE times)

- **Phase 3 PR #4 round 1:** letterhead missing from rendered HTML (custom Jinja print formats don't auto-wrap with Standard's `{{ letter_head|safe }}`).
- **Phase 3 PR #4 round 2:** no fresh-install smoke, no browser visual check, no PDF round-trip done before declaring green.
- **Phase 4 PR #7:** three Notification templates referenced fields that don't exist on their doctypes (`doc.total_royalty`, `doc.title`, `doc.description`), AND `log_outbound_email` rejected `communication_type='Automated Message'` so every Notification-fired email skipped the audit log. **Fixture-import tests passed because Frappe defers Jinja eval until fire time.**
- **Phase 7c PR #14 follow-up:** MYS Branch desk number cards empty for branch staff. Two compounding causes — Custom Number Cards missing `document_type` (Frappe's `has_permission` returns False), and workspace content blocks keyed by Number Card doc name instead of `Workspace Number Card.label` (`block.js` look-up failed). I verified only as `branch.dir@mys.local`, declared "tested in detail", and missed that **Branch Principal / Branch Admin / Branch Accountant share the same workspace but had different `FRANCHISE_ROLE_READS` grants** — so Principal couldn't see the royalty card, Accountant couldn't see the findings card. Caught only after Ali pushed back **again**. Fix: enumerate the user × surface matrix explicitly, and codify it as a script (`scripts/verify_branch_desk_cards.py`).
- **Phase 7d PR #15:** declared "API/HTTP layer covered" with `verify_http_battery` doing `GET /inspection/*` (status + "no access denied" string match) and no browser pass at all — meaning the **checklist runner JS** (apply template → save → submit) and **`POST /admission-enquiry`** were never exercised before pushing. CI was *pending*, not green, when I labeled the slice done. Ali pushed back: *"why you always miss browser testing and fresh install e2e?"* — root causes captured in `## Why I always miss browser + fresh-install browser` below.
- **Phase 11 PR #24:** merged on CI-Playwright-green alone. I admitted afterwards that I had **(a)** never run Playwright locally (just leaned on CI), **(b)** never done a manual dev-site browser walk with screenshots, and **(c)** shipped a spec with gaps — it asserted the three landing pages but skipped the `/branch` dashboard timetable card, the guardian `?student=` filter, and desk `Course Schedule` list scoping. Ali: *"this must also be done for each phase."* These three are now codified as items **5a/5b/5c** below and are **mandatory every phase**, not session-local good intentions.

CI passing means the code compiles and the assertions you happened to write hold — it does **not** mean the feature works.

## Why I always miss browser + fresh-install browser

Three patterns recur — name them so the loophole is closed, not just felt-bad-about:

1. **HTTP-as-proxy-for-browser.** A 200 + absence of "access denied" body says nothing about JS, CSRF, redirects, form POST, hidden state, or whether a button is even visible. **HTTP smoke is not browser smoke.** They are two separate items on the battery.
2. **Battery-as-menu, not checklist.** Mapping a feature to "the most relevant 3–4 items" and assuming the rest are "covered elsewhere" is the bug. The battery is *all 8 items*. If one is genuinely n/a (e.g. PDF when no print format changes), say so **explicitly with one line of justification** — silence is not a skip.
3. **"CI pending" reported as "CI in the test plan."** A test plan that says "CI green" but is sent while CI is `pending` is a status-laundering shortcut. **CI must be terminal-state green** before status is reported, or the message must say "blocking on CI run id X."

## Forbidden substitutions (do not do)

- "HTTP smoke covers the browser case." → **No.** Run the browser.
- "Tests on fresh site, so the fresh-install browser walk isn't needed." → **No.** Unit + HTTP on the fresh site is still not a browser pass on the fresh site.
- "I'll verify in browser later if asked." → **No.** Browser is in the battery for the first commit, not on demand.
- "CI ran Playwright, so I don't need to run it locally." → **No.** That's item #9, not 5a. Run the spec locally too — that's the Phase 11 short.
- "The Playwright spec passed, so the manual browser walk isn't needed." → **No.** 5b is independent of 5a; a spec only asserts what you predicted.
- "I covered the obvious pages." → **No.** 5c demands every surface/variant/filter/list-scope the phase added has an assertion.
- "Out of scope." → **Forbidden mid-verification** (see rule below).
- "Single user is representative." → **No** for any shared surface (workspace, sidebar, portal, form).

## The battery (walk it before claiming ready)

Every PR status message MUST list these items **explicitly** with one of: ✅ (done, evidence), ⏳ (running, with shell/run id), ⛔ (blocked, with reason), or n/a (with one-line justification). No item silently dropped.

1. **Unit tests** — `bench --site SITE run-tests --app myschools` green **locally**, not just on CI.
2. **Lint / pre-commit** — green locally.
3. **Live HTTP smoke** — actually hit the relevant endpoints on the running local site (`http://myschools.localhost:8000`) as Administrator, assert markers in the response. Don't assume `render_template`-style unit tests prove the request path works. **HTTP is not a substitute for #5 — both run.**
4. **Fresh-install smoke** — `bench drop-site test_mys && bench new-site ... && bench install-app myschools && bench migrate` cleanly, no errors. Catches `after_install` vs `after_sync` / `after_migrate` ordering bugs. **Then also tick item #4b.**
4b. **Fresh-install browser pass** — on the same fresh site as #4, log in as at least one role the feature targets and walk the new surface in a real browser (cursor-ide-browser MCP). This is the check that proves the seed path, the install hooks, *and* the JS all hold together for a brand-new site. **Not optional, not "covered by #5 on dev site."**
5. **Browser visual check** — open the relevant pages (`/app/<workspace>`, `/printview?...`, `/portal`, web form POST, etc.) on the **dev site** for every role × surface cell from #8. Screenshots are cheap. For any interactive flow (Web Form POST, JS button, checklist runner), walk the **entire happy path** — not just the landing render. Confirm the side effect (DB row, status change, redirect target). The next three sub-items (**5a/5b/5c**) are each independent battery rows — none of them is satisfied by the other two, and none is satisfied by CI alone.
5a. **Local Playwright run** — run the phase's spec(s) **on your machine** (`cd frappe-bench/apps/myschools && npx playwright test tests/e2e/phaseN_*.spec.ts --reporter=list`) and paste the pass count. "CI ran Playwright" is **not** a substitute — CI green is item #9; this is the local catch *before* you spend CI minutes, and it proves the spec runs against the dev seed too. Reporting "CI covered it" instead of running it locally is the exact Phase 11 short.
5b. **Manual dev-site browser walk + screenshots** — independently of any spec, drive the new surface yourself in the browser (cursor-ide-browser MCP) for the role(s) it targets, and **attach the screenshot path(s)** in the status message. A passing Playwright spec does **not** discharge this — the spec only asserts what you thought to assert; the manual walk is where you *see* the regressions you didn't predict. Embed the screenshots inline so Ali can see them.
5c. **Spec-completeness audit** — before declaring done, enumerate **every surface, variant, and query-param the phase added** and confirm each has a Playwright assertion. Not just the landing pages: dashboard summary cards, `?param=` filters, empty-state vs populated, desk **list-scoping** (does role X see only their rows?), and every nav link the phase introduces. Write the enumeration down in the status message and tick each. A spec that covers "the three obvious pages" while skipping the card / filter / scoping the phase shipped is an incomplete spec — add the missing assertions *in the same PR*.
6. **PDF round-trip** — if a print format ships, generate an actual PDF via `frappe.utils.print_format.download_pdf`. If wkhtmltopdf is broken locally, say so explicitly rather than treating it as "out of scope."
7. **Plan-level verification list** — the plan often lists numbered E2E checks. Walk them, don't skip them.
8. **Role × surface matrix** — for any change that touches a *shared surface* (workspace, sidebar, role perms, portal, dashboard, number card, shortcut, web form), **write the matrix down** before declaring done: every relevant test user × every assertion on that surface, and tick each cell with the actual command/HTTP/browser evidence. Verifying as one user is not "tested in detail." Codify the matrix as a `scripts/verify_*.py` bench-execute script (e.g. `scripts/verify_branch_desk_cards.py`) and re-run it on every related change — future regressions then have a one-line repro.
9. **CI green (terminal state)** — `gh pr checks <N>` reports every required check as `pass`. `pending` / `queued` / `in_progress` is **not** green. If status must be reported before CI completes, the message must say "blocking on CI run id X" rather than implying done.

## Hard procedural rules (because the soft version has failed five times)

- Before pushing the **first commit** on a feature branch, run the full battery locally — not after pushing, not after CI goes green.
- When reporting status to Ali, do not write "ready to merge" (or any synonym) unless you can list, in the same message, the actual battery items run and their results. If not yet run, say *"tests + CI green, still need to run [list]"* — never "ready."
- For Notification/Email Template fixtures specifically, the battery MUST include a Jinja-render-against-real-doc test AND an end-to-end fire smoke (submit a real doc, watch the Communication chain land in `MYS Communication Log`). See [`jinja-render-test`](jinja-render-test.mdc).
- Treat Ali's pushback *"have you tested it?"* / *"are you sure it's tested end to end?"* / *"why you always miss browser?"* as a signal that you shorted the battery — not as a fresh request. Admit the short and run it.
- **"Out of scope" is forbidden mid-verification.** If you notice something broken (an empty card, a missing badge, a 500, a stale field) while walking the battery, it is in scope until Ali explicitly says otherwise — do not paper over it in the wrap-up message.
- **Enumerate the user matrix in writing before claiming done.** For shared surfaces, list every relevant role/user as a checklist in the assistant message; ticking them as evidence comes in is how "tested in detail" is earned. Verifying as a single user on a multi-user surface is a process bug, not a thorough check.
- **Browser + fresh-install browser are not optional.** They are battery items #5 and #4b. The status message MUST list both with evidence (screenshot path, DOM assertion, side-effect confirmation) before "done" / "complete" / "ready". A status message that omits either item is a process bug, regardless of what else passed.
- **Every phase ships the 5a/5b/5c trio — no exceptions.** (5a) local Playwright run with pasted pass count; (5b) manual dev browser walk with **attached screenshots**; (5c) written spec-completeness audit enumerating every surface/variant/filter/list-scope the phase added. "CI covered the browser" discharges **none** of these. If a phase genuinely adds no browser-facing surface (pure backend/cron), say so with one line of justification — but a phase that touches a portal, desk page, card, or nav link never qualifies.
- **Open every PR with the battery checklist pre-filled** in the PR body, even if items are still ⏳. The first comment on the PR thread MUST flip them to ✅ as evidence accrues. Closing the PR with any item not ✅ or n/a-with-justification is a process bug.
- **`gh pr checks` must be terminal-green before status is reported.** `pending` does not count. If the user asks for status while CI is mid-run, the honest answer is "blocking on CI, run id X" — not "tests + CI in the plan."

## Status message template (copy-paste, fill, never omit a row)

When reporting PR status, the message MUST contain this block (renamed if helpful, but all rows present):

```
Battery for PR #N:
  1. Unit tests           — ✅ / ⏳ / ⛔ / n/a (one-line evidence or reason)
  2. Lint / pre-commit    — ✅ / ⏳ / ⛔ / n/a
  3. HTTP smoke (dev)     — ✅ / ⏳ / ⛔ / n/a
  4. Fresh-install smoke  — ✅ / ⏳ / ⛔ / n/a
  4b. Fresh-install BROWSER — ✅ / ⏳ / ⛔ / n/a   ← do not omit
  5. Browser visual (dev, all roles in matrix #8) — ✅ / ⏳ / ⛔ / n/a   ← do not omit
  5a. Local Playwright run — ✅ / ⏳ / ⛔ / n/a (paste pass count; NOT "CI ran it")
  5b. Manual dev browser walk — ✅ / ⏳ / ⛔ / n/a (attach screenshot path(s))
  5c. Spec-completeness audit — ✅ / ⏳ / ⛔ / n/a (enumerate every surface/variant/filter/list-scope)
  6. PDF round-trip       — ✅ / ⏳ / ⛔ / n/a
  7. Plan-level list      — ✅ / ⏳ / ⛔ / n/a
  8. Role × surface matrix — ✅ / ⏳ / ⛔ / n/a (link to verify_*.py)
  9. CI green (terminal)  — ✅ / ⏳ / ⛔ / n/a (gh pr checks N)
```

Any "done" claim that does not include this block has shorted the battery.

## Sibling rule — verify before STARTING work, not just before merging

Before "kicking off" any phase or starting any plan: `git log --oneline -25` on develop AND `ls` the target directories. **The roadmap may have moved on; the work may already be merged.**

This was already missed once — a `feature/shell-phase-1-2` branch was cut to start Phase 1+2 work that had already shipped in PR #3 (`9ad4351 feat(shell): role-aware ERP shell — brand, workspaces, sidebar scoping`). Don't repeat it.

